Privacy Policy – Habitable App
Effective Date: March 25, 2026 Developer: O1E3 Studio

1. Introduction
Welcome to Habitable ("the App"), a habit tracking application developed by O1E3 Studio ("we," "us," or "our"). This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and protect your information when you use our App.

By using the App, you agree to the terms of this Privacy Policy.

2. Information We Collect
2.1 Information You Provide
Habit data: Names, colors, notes, and completion records for habits you create.
All habit data is stored locally on your device and is never uploaded to our servers.
2.2 Automatically Collected Information
We do not collect any analytics or usage data directly. However, our third-party service providers may collect limited non-personal technical information as described below.

2.3 Biometric Data
If you enable the Privacy Lock feature, the App uses your device's biometric hardware (fingerprint, face recognition) or PIN to authenticate access. We do not collect, store, or transmit any biometric data. Authentication is handled entirely by your device's operating system (e.g., Android BiometricPrompt API).

3. Third-Party Services
3.1 RevenueCat (Subscription Management)
We use RevenueCat to manage in-app subscriptions and purchases. RevenueCat may collect:

Device identifiers (e.g., Google Advertising ID)
Purchase transaction data and subscription status
App version and platform information
This data is used solely to validate and manage your premium subscription. RevenueCat does not have access to your habit or personal data.

3.2 Google Play Billing
In-app purchases are processed through Google Play Billing. Payment data is handled entirely by Google and never seen or stored by us.


4. How We Use Your Information
Data	Purpose
Habit tracking data	Core app functionality (stored locally only)
Biometric authentication	App lock / privacy protection (locally only)
Subscription status via RevenueCat	Unlocking premium features
Notification permissions	Sending habit reminders (on-device only)

5. Data Storage & Security
All habit data, streak records, and settings are stored locally on your device using a SQLite database (sqflite).
No personal data is transmitted to our servers.
Subscription status is synchronized with RevenueCat's servers over encrypted HTTPS connections.
We implement industry-standard security measures to protect any limited data we do handle.

6. Data Retention & Deletion
All your habit data is deleted when you uninstall the App from your device.
To cancel your subscription or manage your billing data, visit your Google Play account settings or the RevenueCat customer portal.
We do not retain any personal data on our own servers.

7. Children's Privacy
The App is not directed at children under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect any personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided us with personal information, please contact us and we will delete it promptly.

8. Permissions Used
Permission	Reason
USE_BIOMETRIC / USE_FINGERPRINT	Privacy Lock feature (optional, user-controlled)
POST_NOTIFICATIONS	Habit reminder notifications (optional)
SCHEDULE_EXACT_ALARM	Precise daily habit reminders
RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED	Restore notification schedules after device restart
INTERNET	RevenueCat subscription validation
BILLING	Google Play in-app purchases

9. User Rights
You have the right to:

Access the data stored locally on your device at any time through the App.
Delete all your data by uninstalling the App.
Opt out of RevenueCat data collection by not subscribing to Premium features.
Disable biometric authentication at any time in Settings.

10. Changes to This Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be reflected by an updated Effective Date at the top of this page. Continued use of the App after changes constitutes your acceptance of the new policy.

